orth>കന്നടിക്ക</orth></form> <sense><def xml:lang="en">to cultivate hill-</def> <def xml:lang="en"><lb facs="#p300_r63_l001"/>ground.</def></sense> </entry><entry type="derived"><form><orth><lb facs="#p300_r65_l001"/>കന്നൻ</orth></form> <sense n="1"><lbl type="senseNumber">1.</lbl> <def xml:lang="en">mountaineer; ignorant.</def> <def xml:lang="en"><lb facs="#p300_r67_l001"/>on tiptoe</def></sense> <etym>(√ കുന്തുക)</etym> <sense n="3"><lbl type="senseNumber">3.</lbl> <def xml:lang="en">a kind</def> <cit type="example"><quote xml:lang="ml"><lb facs="#p300_r69_l001"/>കു. വാഴ</quote><bibl>V1.</bibl></cit> </sense> </entry><entry type="derived"><form><orth><lb facs="#p300_r71_l001"/>കന്നമുക്കി</orth></form> <sense><def xml:lang="en">"pressing hills down" a</def></sense> </entry><entry type="derived"><form><orth><lb facs="#p300_r73_l001"/>കുന്നം</orth></form> <etym>a M. (a T. കന്റം)</etym> <sense><def xml:lang="en">mountain</def> <cit type="example"><quote xml:lang="ml"><lb facs="#p300_r75_l001"/>ത്തമ്മ, ചെറുകുന്നം പ്രവൃത്തി</quote><bibl>TR</bibl></cit>  <note><lb facs="#p300_r77_l001"/>ഴൻ</note> <def xml:lang="en">mountain splitter, a title.</def> <note>J</note></sense></entry><entry xml:id="p300_e19" facs="#p300_r79_l001 #p300_r81_l001" type="derived"><form type="lemma"><orth><lb facs="#p300_r79_l001"/>കന്നലക്കോൻ</orth></form> <note>(അല)</note> <sense><def xml:lang="en">Lord over hil</def> <def xml:lang="en"><lb facs="#p300_r81_l001"/>Tāmūri;</def> <xr type="syn">also കന്നിന്നു കോനാരി</xr></sense></entry><entry xml:id="p300_e20" facs="#p300_r83_l001 #p300_r85_l001 #p300_r87_l001" type="derived"><form type="lemma"><orth><lb facs="#p300_r83_l001"/>കന്നിക്ക</orth></form> <sense n="1"><lbl type="senseNumber">1.</lbl> <def xml:lang="en">to pile up, heap up.</def> <cit type="example"><quote xml:lang="ml">ത</quote></cit> <cit type="example"><quote xml:lang="ml"><lb facs="#p300_r85_l001"/>കിടക്കുന്നു</quote><bibl>V1.</bibl></cit>  <cit type="example"><quote xml:lang="ml">വെള്ള